{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793454032,"nonce":"MbSRTtSkBG6lcwZsQ9r7WeDQqlg=","title":"Step images with a named non-root USER fail CreateContainerConfigError","message":"Found 2026-10-31 by the live Forgejo tier (just forgejo-verify, case an_installed_library_runs_and_a_yank_refuses_its_rerun).\n\nSteps run with runAsNonRoot: true and no runAsUser (scarab-executor-k8s step_security_context, lib.rs ~4844). The kubelet refuses an image whose USER is a NAME, since it cannot check that the name is not root. curlimages/curl (USER curl_user, uid 100) fails every launch with CreateContainerConfigError; the Step fails with no message that says why.\n\nHit by: .scarab/lib/notify.yaml (dogfood's notify step; rarely runs: behind deploy + a manual gate) — fixed on fix/live-test-step0 (edd63788) by switching to an image with a numeric user. Still in: docs usage/pipeline-syntax.mdx:646 (image: curlimages/curl in the plugin-gate example).\n\nSteps have no security.run_as_user (services do: ServiceSpec.run_as_user). Options for the owner:\n(a) a self-service step security.run_as_user (a non-zero uid is not an escalation), set as runAsUser;\n(b) when a Step Pod sits in CreateContainerConfigError, fail the Attempt with the kubelet's message (e.g. 'image has non-numeric user ... cannot verify user is non-root') and a hint;\n(c) both. (b) is worth doing regardless: today the cause is only visible in kubectl describe.","files":null}]}